---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BuyerSpec from "../../../components/BuyerSpec.astro";
import AtAGlance from "../../../components/AtAGlance.astro";
import { buildOffers, priceLine } from "../../../data/product-offers";

const productUrl = "https://drychillis.com/products/seven-star-chilli/";
const productOffers = buildOffers("seven-star-chilli", productUrl);

const buyerSpec = [
  { param: "Product form", value: "Confirm specification" },
  { param: "Variety", value: "Seven-Star Chilli" },
  { param: "Heat level (SHU)", value: "20,000–50,000" },
  { param: "ASTA colour value", value: "Confirm specification" },
  { param: "Mesh size", value: "Confirm specification" },
  { param: "Moisture", value: "<13%" },
  { param: "Processing", value: "Confirm specification" },
  { param: "Certifications", value: "ISO 9001 & HACCP standard — BRC, Halal, Kosher on request" },
];

const glanceFacts = [
  { label: "Heat level", value: "20,000–50,000 SHU" },
  { label: "Region", value: "Shandong, Shanxi" },
  { label: "Best for", value: "Snack seasoning, hot-pot bases" },
  { label: "Certifications", value: "ISO 9001 & HACCP" },
];

const productJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  "@id": "https://drychillis.com/products/seven-star-chilli/#product",
  "name": "Seven-Star Chilli",
  "description": "Seven-Star pepper — high-heat chilli at 20,000–50,000 SHU from Shandong and Shanxi, for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. China manufacturer, ISO 9001 & HACCP.",
  "image": ["https://drychillis.com/images/products/chilli-whole.jpg"],
  "url": "https://drychillis.com/products/seven-star-chilli/",
  "sku": "TENDA-SEVEN-STAR-CHILLI",
  "category": "Spices and Seasonings",
  "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": "Tenda Peppers" },
  "manufacturer": { "@id": "https://drychillis.com/#organization" },
  ...(productOffers ? { "offers": productOffers } : {}),
  "additionalProperty": [
    { "@type": "PropertyValue", "name": "Heat Level (SHU)", "value": "20,000–50,000", "unitText": "SHU" },
    { "@type": "PropertyValue", "name": "Region", "value": "Shandong, Shanxi" },
    { "@type": "PropertyValue", "name": "Best For", "value": "Snack seasoning, hot-pot bases" }
  ]
};

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Seven-Star chilli?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Seven-Star is a high-heat chilli at 20,000–50,000 SHU from Shandong and Shanxi, used mainly for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. It is one of the workhorse high-heat varieties alongside Sanying and Zidantou."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How hot is Seven-Star pepper?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Seven-Star sits in the high-heat band at 20,000–50,000 SHU — strong and lingering, above medium varieties like Xian and Jinta (10,000–20,000) and below the extra-hot Jixin, Xiaomi and Chilli King (over 50,000). Specify a precise SHU window, not just \"high heat\"."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Seven-Star pepper used for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Seven-Star is a standard for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases, and it is milled with Sanying and Zidantou into chilli powder. Name the variety and the SHU window to lock batch-to-batch consistency."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Seven-Star Chilli — 20,000–50,000 SHU | Tenda Peppers"
  description="Seven-Star pepper — high-heat chilli at 20,000–50,000 SHU from Shandong and Shanxi, for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. China manufacturer, ISO 9001 & HACCP."
  jsonLd={[productJsonLd, faqJsonLd]}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#6b5a54;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/products/dried-chillies/">Dried Chillies</a> &rsaquo; Seven-Star
    </nav>
    <h1>Seven-Star Chilli</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A high-heat chilli at 20,000–50,000 SHU from Shandong and Shanxi — a workhorse for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases.
    </p>
    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> Seven-Star is a high-heat chilli (20,000–50,000 SHU) from Shandong and Shanxi, commonly milled for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. It sits in the same band as Sanying and Zidantou — the band where heat defines the product but does not drown the other flavours.
    </div>
    <AtAGlance facts={glanceFacts} />
    <div class="product-media">
      <img src="/images/products/chilli-whole.jpg" alt="Whole dried chillies" width="1400" height="1050" loading="eager" />
    </div>
    <p class="product-price" style="font-weight:600;color:#8a1c1c;margin:10px 0 0;">Price confirmed on quotation — MOQ, packing and specification agreed before order.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is Seven-Star chilli?</h2>
    <p>
      Seven-Star is a high-heat chilli at 20,000–50,000 SHU, grown in Shandong and Shanxi. On the <a href="/heat-levels/high-heat/">high heat</a> page it sits alongside Sanying and Zidantou as one of the workhorse varieties in the 20,000–50,000 SHU band — hot enough to define a product, mild enough to keep other flavours in play.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Heat (SHU)</strong></td><td>20,000–50,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Region</strong></td><td>Shandong, Shanxi</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Best for</strong></td><td>Snack seasoning, hot-pot bases</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is Seven-Star pepper used for?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Snack seasoning</li>
      <li>Hot-pot bases</li>
      <li>Chilli powder (milled with Sanying and Zidantou)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Seven-Star vs Sanying vs Zidantou</h2>
    <p>
      Sanying (Tianying) and Zidantou are the classic hot-sauce varieties at 20,000–50,000 SHU; Seven-Star is common in snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. Heat, colour and flavour vary independently, so name the variety and a precise SHU window — the variety name is what locks batch-to-batch consistency.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Seven-Star Chilli by the numbers</h2>
    <p>
      Seven-Star runs 20,000–50,000 SHU — roughly 40–100 times hotter than sweet paprika (under 500 SHU) and one band below the extra-hot Jixin, Xiaomi and Chilli King (over 50,000 SHU).
    </p>
    <p class="data-note">
      Heat values are representative per variety. Confirm your exact SHU window, form and mesh when
      you inquire.
    </p>

    <BuyerSpec rows={buyerSpec} />

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is Seven-Star chilli?</h3>
      <p>Seven-Star is a high-heat chilli at 20,000–50,000 SHU from Shandong and Shanxi, used mainly for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases. It is one of the workhorse high-heat varieties alongside Sanying and Zidantou.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>How hot is Seven-Star pepper?</h3>
      <p>Seven-Star sits in the high-heat band at 20,000–50,000 SHU — strong and lingering, above medium varieties like Xian and Jinta (10,000–20,000) and below the extra-hot Jixin, Xiaomi and Chilli King (over 50,000). Specify a precise SHU window, not just "high heat".</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is Seven-Star pepper used for?</h3>
      <p>Seven-Star is a standard for snack seasoning and hot-pot bases, and it is milled with Sanying and Zidantou into chilli powder. Name the variety and the SHU window to lock batch-to-batch consistency.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:32px;">
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Request Seven-Star Quotation</a>
      <a class="cta cta-outline" href="/products/dried-chillies/" style="margin-left:8px;">Dried Chillies →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
